{# Rendered by ops/ansible/roles/node-exporter — ADR 1128 §3.

   THE DENOMINATOR. Before this file, nothing in the repository declared how
   big any host's pipe was: link_capacity / uplink_mbps / bandwidth_mbps /
   capacity_bps all returned zero hits across ops/ and docs/design/, so
   "percent of available pipe" had nothing to divide by.

   Values are BYTES per second, not bits: Prometheus convention is base units
   and promtool lints the bits form. Operators declare mbps in group_vars
   (which is how links are sold and specced) and the conversion happens here,
   once. Every consumer multiplies by 8 for display.

   It is a DECLARED fact and says so. `source` is the honesty carrier:
     measured  — someone ran a throughput test and wrote the result down
     declared  — the number a contract, ISP plan or NIC spec says
     unknown   — nobody has said. The dashboard then shows raw bytes/s and the
                 words "capacity not declared" rather than a fabricated %.

   Deriving capacity from observed peak was rejected: peak observed is a FLOOR
   on capacity, not a measure of it, and a link never driven hard would report
   a small pipe and then show 95% utilisation under a trivial load. #}
# HELP goat_link_capacity_bytes_per_second Declared link capacity in bytes per second. Declared, not measured, unless the source label says measured. See ADR 1128.
# TYPE goat_link_capacity_bytes_per_second gauge
{% set cap = node_exporter_link_capacity %}
{% set src = cap.source | default('unknown') %}
{% if src != 'unknown' and (cap.down_mbps | default(0) | float) > 0 %}
goat_link_capacity_bytes_per_second{direction="rx",source="{{ src }}"} {{ (cap.down_mbps | float * 1000000 / 8) | int }}
{% endif %}
{% if src != 'unknown' and (cap.up_mbps | default(0) | float) > 0 %}
goat_link_capacity_bytes_per_second{direction="tx",source="{{ src }}"} {{ (cap.up_mbps | float * 1000000 / 8) | int }}
{% endif %}
# HELP goat_link_capacity_declared 1 when this host has a usable capacity declaration. 0 means every percent-of-link panel must refuse to render a number for this host rather than assume a default pipe.
# TYPE goat_link_capacity_declared gauge
goat_link_capacity_declared{source="{{ src }}"} {{ 1 if src != 'unknown' and ((cap.down_mbps | default(0) | float) > 0 or (cap.up_mbps | default(0) | float) > 0) else 0 }}
{% if cap.asserted_on is defined and cap.asserted_on %}
# HELP goat_link_capacity_asserted_timestamp_seconds When the declaration was last affirmed. A capacity nobody has re-checked in a year is a stale claim, and the dashboard ages it visibly rather than trusting it forever.
# TYPE goat_link_capacity_asserted_timestamp_seconds gauge
goat_link_capacity_asserted_timestamp_seconds {{ (cap.asserted_on | to_datetime('%Y-%m-%d')).timestamp() | int }}
{% endif %}
